r/id #uuid "48ad9111-5ff9-5808-834a-73627abed3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438216} {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438217} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d06f78-7466-5d54-950d-cb989daacc0e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438218} {:answer/id #uuid "00a2f1ae-0f2a-55b3-bef4-eabad652d111" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438218} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c704ed7-9a63-5c1b-90d0-bdb2e302d80f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8099f21-9137-5121-a075-a61a4c5ae84b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36039" :question/problem "![](images/93/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-4,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,1)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/cb/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5ab6900-c8da-56de-b62a-bf3a1d4d10d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122709} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d89c4b-603f-53ac-a7b7-b89c17fd5c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122710} {:answer/id #uuid "4693a105-893c-5ac9-9b6c-e651dc075271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122711} {:answer/id #uuid "5e948606-25c1-55c6-9bde-c9158bb85ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122712} {:answer/id #uuid "766b5449-7ecc-5a19-ba23-f9f7d5c3156f" :answer/type {: